        "original_id": "304b4117-93d0-5f2b-95e3-d5d46d55d9d9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Randall Park, Kim Jong-Un, Danny Chung, Eddie Huang, Louis Huang, Seth Rogen, Evan Goldberg\n- Works: The Interview, Veep, Fresh Off the Boat, Vice documentary\n- Roles: actor, comedian, writer, director, governor, restaurateur\n\nFacts:\n- Randall Park was born on March 23, 1974, and he is an American actor, comedian, writer, and director.\n- A Vice documentary that was shot in 2012 heavily inspired the 2014 film The Interview.\n- The Interview is a 2014 American action comedy film directed by Seth Rogen and Evan Goldberg.\n- In the 2014 film The Interview, Randall Park played Kim Jong-Un.\n- In Veep, Randall Park played Minnesota governor Danny Chung.\n- Beginning in 2015, Randall Park portrayed Louis Huang, Eddie Huang's father and an American restaurateur, in ABC's television show Fresh Off the Boat.",
